#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aa-autolink — inline-link bare references in narrative prose.

Many narrative pages name papers, statutes, authors, and organisations
without hyperlinking. Adam called this out on /the-debate/recognition-vs-critique
(26+ evidence pages had 0 inline links despite 1000-9000 words of body).

This script scans every .md body and, for each pattern, replaces the FIRST
occurrence per page with an inline markdown link. Frontmatter, code blocks,
existing markdown links, and the AA-CITE/AA-CROSSLINK appended blocks are
all skipped. Idempotent: re-running produces no further changes once each
first-occurrence is linked.

Run order in aa-sync: after aa-cite + aa-crosslink (which append bottom
blocks), so the autolinker can skip those blocks unambiguously.
"""
